WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.983
Local large-language-model infrastructure is the hardware, runtime software, storage, interfaces, controls, and operating practices used to run model inference on systems you control.

00:00:11.983 --> 00:00:21.032
The model may live on a laptop, workstation, gaming PC, mini PC, server, or managed private environment.

00:00:21.032 --> 00:00:27.146
Local inference sends prompts to a model running in that environment.

00:00:27.146 --> 00:00:36.195
A cloud API sends requests to an external provider under its service, security, pricing, and data-handling model.

00:00:36.195 --> 00:00:43.287
Hybrid designs may route different workloads according to sensitivity, quality, cost, or availability.

00:00:43.287 --> 00:00:53.314
Hardware choices include CPUs, discrete GPUs, unified-memory systems such as Apple Silicon, system memory, storage, networking, power, and cooling.

00:00:53.314 --> 00:01:01.385
Software choices include model formats, runtimes, drivers, user interfaces, local APIs, monitoring, and access control.

00:01:01.385 --> 00:01:09.944
Local operation can improve data control, offline capability, experimentation, customization, and cost predictability for steady workloads.

00:01:09.944 --> 00:01:19.482
It also transfers responsibility for hardware limits, software updates, security, backups, availability, and model governance to the operator.

00:01:19.482 --> 00:01:23.151
Performance depends on the complete configuration.

00:01:23.151 --> 00:01:36.112
Model architecture, parameter count, quantization, context length, prompt size, batch behavior, concurrency, runtime, acceleration backend, and cooling can matter as much as the device name.

00:01:36.112 --> 00:01:41.737
The right question is not whether local is always better.

00:01:41.737 --> 00:01:53.721
It is whether a measured local system meets the task's quality, privacy, latency, throughput, cost, and operational requirements more effectively than available alternatives.
